Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.908 --> 00:00:03.916
- Opportunity.

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:04.920
- Opportunity.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.919
- Opportunity.

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:06.925
- Opportunity.

00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:07.758
- Opportunities.

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:09.338
- I went and created
opportunity for myself.

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:11.531
- Hello Believe Nation, my
name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:11.531 --> 00:00:14.189
My one word is believe and I believe that

00:00:14.189 --> 00:00:15.972
entrepreneurs are going to solve all

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:17.976
of the worlds major problems.

00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:19.815
So, to help you in your journey today,

00:00:19.815 --> 00:00:23.595
we're going to learn how you
cannot miss opportunities.

00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:25.202
And as always, as your watching,

00:00:25.202 --> 00:00:27.048
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:27.048 --> 00:00:28.823
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:31.321
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired,

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:34.212
and when you write it down,
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:35.605
with yourself as well.

00:00:35.605 --> 00:00:36.835
Enjoy.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:40.585
(inspiring orchestra music)

00:00:48.411 --> 00:00:50.663
- Many of you have a
very small opportunity

00:00:50.663 --> 00:00:53.364
and you're not taking
advantage of that opportunity

00:00:53.364 --> 00:00:55.364
because you're not thinking
about the next opportunity.

00:00:55.364 --> 00:00:56.548
You're looking at this as small.

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:57.988
No, this is the gateway.

00:00:57.988 --> 00:00:59.124
Like, this is the first one, right?

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:01.828
So, you got to ask yourself
this question, like,

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.578
how do you keep that fire?

00:01:03.578 --> 00:01:04.926
You know how you keep it?

00:01:04.926 --> 00:01:06.957
You keep putting different
opportunities in front of you.

00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:08.701
You keep setting different opportunities.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.376
Anybody know who this is?

00:01:10.376 --> 00:01:11.209
Yeah, you should.

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:12.134
He in the Big 10.

00:01:12.134 --> 00:01:12.967
He gave us the business.

00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:13.800
You should know who he is.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.188
Yogi Ferrell.

00:01:15.188 --> 00:01:16.065
Didn't get drafted.

00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:18.003
Didn't' get drafted to the NBA.

00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:20.613
Didn't get drafted but they just,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.446
something happened the other day.

00:01:21.446 --> 00:01:22.433
The Dallas Mavericks needed a player.

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:24.364
They gave my man a 10-day contract.

00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:26.176
How much did he make?

00:01:26.176 --> 00:01:27.757
They gave my man $100,000 dollars.

00:01:27.757 --> 00:01:29.196
How much LeBron making?

00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:30.029
A million!

00:01:30.029 --> 00:01:30.862
They gave my man,

00:01:30.862 --> 00:01:32.712
"Look for 10 days, we just
want you to play for us.

00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:33.782
"Somebody got hurt.

00:01:33.782 --> 00:01:35.022
"We are going to bring
you in for 10 days."

00:01:35.022 --> 00:01:36.647
You know say, you got 10-days.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:37.647
Ride the bench.

00:01:37.647 --> 00:01:39.816
You know, do your thing,
but you only got 10 days.

00:01:39.816 --> 00:01:41.686
Don't get your hopes up.

00:01:41.686 --> 00:01:42.889
My man, be coming in,

00:01:42.889 --> 00:01:45.115
I'm talkin' about Trick.

00:01:45.115 --> 00:01:46.116
Boom.

00:01:46.116 --> 00:01:47.611
No only three pointers like daggers.

00:01:47.611 --> 00:01:48.782
Two seconds.

00:01:48.782 --> 00:01:49.783
Boom.

00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:50.865
The 10-day contract,

00:01:50.865 --> 00:01:52.860
they turnin' this boy
about to get a contract.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.906
What are you doing with your opportunity?

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:55.904
We all get one.

00:01:55.904 --> 00:01:57.576
We all get the 10-day contract.

00:01:57.576 --> 00:01:59.155
But, the question is,
will that 10-day contract

00:01:59.155 --> 00:02:00.153
turn into a year contract?

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.964
Will it turn into a two year contract?

00:02:01.964 --> 00:02:03.874
You think Yogi Ferrell is the only one

00:02:03.874 --> 00:02:04.765
who's got the opportunity to come

00:02:04.765 --> 00:02:06.092
from a developmental league and play?

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:06.925
Nope.

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:08.152
You think other people
doing what he doing?

00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:08.985
Nope. Why?

00:02:08.985 --> 00:02:10.236
Because they weren't prepared for it.

00:02:10.236 --> 00:02:11.374
What are you doing in the dark?

00:02:11.374 --> 00:02:12.883
When nobody's watching?

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:14.830
What are you doing in the dark?

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.015
10-day contract!

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:19.071
But, he didn't come in and
say, "I only got 10 days."

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:20.975
That's what some of ya'll on.

00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:23.400
Oh, since I only got 10
days, I might as well

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.957
only give 10 days worth of effort.

00:02:24.957 --> 00:02:27.252
I might as well only give
10 days worth of energy.

00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:28.702
Yogi Ferrell was like,

00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:31.198
"I'm about to act like
this might be my last shot.

00:02:31.198 --> 00:02:33.520
"I'm about to act like I'm starting.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.353
"I'm about to act like LeBron.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.265
"I'm about to act like Kyrie.

00:02:36.265 --> 00:02:37.961
"I'm about to act like Steph Curry.

00:02:37.961 --> 00:02:40.082
"When you put me in the
game, I'm tellin' you,

00:02:40.082 --> 00:02:41.556
"I'm about to murder 'em."

00:02:41.556 --> 00:02:43.375
And at the 10-day, he's
been murderin' 'em.

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:45.921
He's been on ESPN almost every day.

00:02:45.921 --> 00:02:48.244
All they talk about, Yogi Ferrell.

00:02:48.244 --> 00:02:52.081
I'm talking about NBA
TV, ESPN One, ESPN Two

00:02:52.081 --> 00:02:53.602
like Spanish ESPN!

00:02:53.602 --> 00:02:55.600
So, ya'll got to understand something.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.738
What was Yogi doing before?

00:02:57.738 --> 00:03:00.235
What was Yogi doing before he
got that opportunity, ya'll?

00:03:00.235 --> 00:03:02.421
He was preparing for it.

00:03:02.421 --> 00:03:05.719
You don't get in the game
and score like he scored.

00:03:05.719 --> 00:03:07.445
So, he said, "So what I
didn't make the league.

00:03:07.445 --> 00:03:08.501
"So what?

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.851
"They can't stop me from practicing.

00:03:10.851 --> 00:03:12.916
"They can't stop me from
getting up in the morning

00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:14.113
"and running drills."

00:03:14.113 --> 00:03:15.747
So, the problem with most of you is,

00:03:15.747 --> 00:03:16.911
you have an opportunity.

00:03:16.911 --> 00:03:17.939
You wrote it down.

00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:19.033
You wrote it down right here.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:19.866
Opportunity.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:20.699
They gave me an opportunity.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:21.830
They gave me a shot.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.525
Somebody gave me a GED.

00:03:23.525 --> 00:03:25.894
I turned that GED into a four-year degree.

00:03:25.894 --> 00:03:27.560
Somebody gave me a four-year degree.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.118
I turned it into a Master's degree.

00:03:29.118 --> 00:03:30.664
Somebody gave me a Master's degree.

00:03:30.664 --> 00:03:32.152
I turned it into a PhD.

00:03:32.152 --> 00:03:34.392
You got the opportunity,
what you doing with it?

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:36.247
Opportunity is coming.

00:03:36.247 --> 00:03:37.875
Will you be ready when it comes?

00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:40.504
- What if I offered you
1.25 million dollars

00:03:40.504 --> 00:03:41.736
to sell the whole company?

00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:44.589
- Mark, you're saying
screw the other sharks.

00:03:44.589 --> 00:03:45.767
- Yep.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:46.678
I like what you guys are doing.

00:03:46.678 --> 00:03:48.983
I want you to come back
to me with a percentage.

00:03:48.983 --> 00:03:50.916
I don't want you to
even talk to these guys.

00:03:50.916 --> 00:03:53.412
- You're asking him to
take that option with you

00:03:53.412 --> 00:03:54.790
right now and ignore us?
- Yep.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.068
- You're not a very nice guy.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.623
- It's not about me being wonderful

00:03:57.623 --> 00:03:59.208
- No, no, I have that title, thank you.

00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:01.092
- It's about making a
business decision, right?

00:04:01.092 --> 00:04:03.079
- Hi, I'm Mark Cuban,
I'm a bully, look at me.

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:04.212
- What's that about, Mark?

00:04:04.212 --> 00:04:06.643
- Like I said, guys,
you got to pay to play.

00:04:06.643 --> 00:04:08.088
- There's tension in this room.

00:04:08.088 --> 00:04:08.921
I can feel it.

00:04:08.921 --> 00:04:09.754
- It's offensive.

00:04:09.754 --> 00:04:10.587
- You got a shot here, right?

00:04:10.587 --> 00:04:12.446
Don't let these guys drag you down.

00:04:12.446 --> 00:04:13.279
- Are you really interested in this?

00:04:13.279 --> 00:04:14.689
- I like the idea.

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:17.754
- You really think cooking
bacon bedside is a good idea?

00:04:17.754 --> 00:04:19.170
- I love your passion.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.410
I love your knowledge.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.243
- I'm waiting for the but.

00:04:21.243 --> 00:04:22.320
- Yeah, there's a but coming.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.671
- You got a 24 second shot,
Clark, 750,000 dollars.

00:04:25.671 --> 00:04:26.631
- I've never seen greed like that.

00:04:26.631 --> 00:04:27.729
That's unbelievable greed.

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:29.364
- You broke up with your potential partner

00:04:29.364 --> 00:04:30.771
without even looking at him.

00:04:30.771 --> 00:04:31.604
- You're a savage.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.792
- I'm just a lean, mean
shark machine, Baby!

00:04:34.792 --> 00:04:37.080
If I say yes to whatever your counter is,

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.200
you have to tell me that
you will say yes immediately

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.572
and we have deal.

00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:41.885
- 100,000 dollars

00:04:41.885 --> 00:04:42.718
- Wait a minute.

00:04:42.718 --> 00:04:43.578
- For 20% equity.

00:04:43.578 --> 00:04:45.402
- Argh!
- Done, done and done.

00:04:45.402 --> 00:04:46.235
- Crap!

00:04:46.235 --> 00:04:47.068
- Did you like that, Barbara?

00:04:47.068 --> 00:04:49.004
- I don't like it one bit.
(sharks laughing)

00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:50.002
That was so damn smart.

00:04:50.002 --> 00:04:51.614
- No but, that's a compliment to you.

00:04:51.614 --> 00:04:54.043
- Barbara, I screwed you,
but it's a compliment to you.

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.605
- I feel really good about it.

00:04:55.605 --> 00:04:56.610
- For every problem,

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:00.469
the problem itself presents an opportunity

00:05:00.469 --> 00:05:01.828
that dwarfs the problem.

00:05:01.828 --> 00:05:05.555
And that is to say, that
if I had only looked

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.210
at my failure with the audio book

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:10.069
and viewed it as a failure
in the product, let's say,

00:05:10.069 --> 00:05:11.401
and not in the process,

00:05:11.401 --> 00:05:13.049
I wouldn't have taken away much.

00:05:13.049 --> 00:05:15.324
Instead, I realized that
my approach wasn't right.

00:05:15.324 --> 00:05:17.129
Fixed my approach and that has led

00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:18.360
to a lot of great successes.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.860
- Success is born out of luck.

00:05:22.032 --> 00:05:24.564
It's awareness of mind that take advantage

00:05:24.564 --> 00:05:26.364
of that opportunity.

00:05:26.364 --> 00:05:29.978
You will all become
fronted with opportunity.

00:05:29.978 --> 00:05:32.286
You must take advantage of it.

00:05:32.286 --> 00:05:35.272
Because If you don't take
advantage of your opportunity

00:05:35.272 --> 00:05:37.130
you'll never realize your dreams.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.719
Whether you want them or
not is the irrelevance.

00:05:39.719 --> 00:05:43.252
You don't know that until you achieve it.

00:05:43.252 --> 00:05:46.760
- I grew up watching movies
and imagining myself on screen.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:51.153
So, aside from the very
serious things that I do,

00:05:51.153 --> 00:05:54.780
I will occasionally do a
Snakes On A Plane because,

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.863
(audience laughing)

00:05:59.144 --> 00:06:01.433
those are the kinds of movies
I like when I was a kid.

00:06:01.433 --> 00:06:03.831
I always wanted to see myself in a movie

00:06:03.831 --> 00:06:05.717
with a bunch of snakes.

00:06:05.717 --> 00:06:09.550
And I'm still trying to
find the right slasher

00:06:10.582 --> 00:06:12.343
movie to do because,
I like slasher movies.

00:06:12.343 --> 00:06:15.485
And I'm still, I did
things like Deep Blue Sea

00:06:15.485 --> 00:06:17.135
because I wanted to run from
something that had big teeth.

00:06:17.135 --> 00:06:19.074
And all that kind of stuff.

00:06:19.074 --> 00:06:20.989
So, I'm not that serious about it.

00:06:20.989 --> 00:06:23.706
You know, I really think
movies should be fun and

00:06:23.706 --> 00:06:25.375
I think they should be entertaining.

00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:27.166
If I want to teach you something,

00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:30.954
I'll do a documentary
but, I do this because

00:06:30.954 --> 00:06:32.024
it feeds me.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.545
It feeds my artistic sense.

00:06:33.545 --> 00:06:35.641
A lot of people think
I do too many movies.

00:06:35.641 --> 00:06:37.914
I read an article on
PBS today about me doing

00:06:37.914 --> 00:06:41.069
too many movies but,
you know, writers get up

00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:42.070
and write everyday.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.523
Painters get up and paint everyday.

00:06:43.523 --> 00:06:46.051
Actors only have so many
acting opportunities

00:06:46.051 --> 00:06:47.054
in a life time.

00:06:47.054 --> 00:06:48.907
I'm going to take mine as they come and

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:52.308
do as many movies as I can
before I'm up out of here.

00:06:52.308 --> 00:06:55.762
- I remember two years ago
when the producer offer

00:06:55.762 --> 00:06:58.757
me to play the bad guy, the villain.

00:06:58.757 --> 00:07:01.570
Little red man for and I say,

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:04.672
"Oh, I made 25 movies in Hong Kong.

00:07:04.672 --> 00:07:07.040
"I never play the villain so, I don't know

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.729
"my audience, what's their reaction when

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:10.832
"they heard the news."

00:07:10.832 --> 00:07:13.598
Said, "Don't worry, here is the good guy."

00:07:13.598 --> 00:07:16.316
He offer another movie, Romeo Must Die.

00:07:16.316 --> 00:07:19.147
So, one bad guy, one good guy.

00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:22.344
You can work. You have special skill.

00:07:22.344 --> 00:07:24.039
You can make money for the studio.

00:07:24.039 --> 00:07:28.747
Now in the future, right now,
maybe better than before.

00:07:28.747 --> 00:07:31.270
I have a little bit of chance, can chose,

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:33.961
what kind of story I really want to make.

00:07:33.961 --> 00:07:37.319
I hope in the future I
have more chance to chose

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:40.478
what kind of story I really want to make,

00:07:40.478 --> 00:07:42.624
what kind of story I don't want to make.

00:07:42.624 --> 00:07:43.457
- We'd only been on the, 32, I think

00:07:43.457 --> 00:07:46.699
we hadn't even done 50 shows.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:47.532
- Wow

00:07:47.532 --> 00:07:50.290
- And so, I called Jon Stewart and I said,

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:54.457
"John, I just got invited for
the correspondence dinner.

00:07:56.986 --> 00:07:59.319
"Do you think should do it?"

00:08:00.778 --> 00:08:03.087
and he said, "What? Like to attend?"

00:08:03.087 --> 00:08:04.904
and I said, "No, they want me."

00:08:04.904 --> 00:08:05.931
He goes, "They want you to be the guy?"

00:08:05.931 --> 00:08:07.323
(laughter)

00:08:07.323 --> 00:08:08.460
"Like to stand next to the President?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.727
Do they know what you do?"

00:08:09.727 --> 00:08:12.123
and I said, "I don't know."

00:08:12.123 --> 00:08:13.504
and I said, "I think I have to do it."

00:08:13.504 --> 00:08:14.891
He goes, "You have to do it."

00:08:14.891 --> 00:08:16.077
- You have to do it.
- Like, right now,

00:08:16.077 --> 00:08:17.238
you have to do it.

00:08:17.238 --> 00:08:19.830
So, don't pay attention
to the approval ratings

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.082
that say that 68 percent of American's

00:08:22.082 --> 00:08:24.564
disapprove of the job this man is doing.

00:08:24.564 --> 00:08:28.148
I ask you this, does that
not also logically mean

00:08:28.148 --> 00:08:32.900
that 68 percent approve
of the job he's not doing?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:36.432
(audience laughter)

00:08:36.432 --> 00:08:37.682
Think about it.

00:08:38.563 --> 00:08:39.850
I haven't

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:42.106
- You know, each day
looks very, very different

00:08:42.106 --> 00:08:45.370
and truthfully that's part of
what I'm so passionate about.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.021
I think more than being a developer,

00:08:48.021 --> 00:08:50.854
more than having my own fashion brands,

00:08:50.854 --> 00:08:53.815
I think of myself as an
entrepreneur who keeps

00:08:53.815 --> 00:08:57.169
my eye open for exciting opportunities and

00:08:57.169 --> 00:09:00.536
you have to have band
width in your schedule,

00:09:00.536 --> 00:09:02.501
despite how busy you are, you have to have

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:04.696
a little bit of space to be able to take

00:09:04.696 --> 00:09:08.645
that meeting that's not
as strategically relevant

00:09:08.645 --> 00:09:09.991
to everything on your plate.

00:09:09.991 --> 00:09:12.021
So, it is important to
be surrounded by people

00:09:12.021 --> 00:09:15.856
that you trust and it's important to spend

00:09:15.856 --> 00:09:18.613
your time wisely to
enable you to find that

00:09:18.613 --> 00:09:19.960
next opportunity.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.410
- I used to do make up
effects for my stuff.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:25.466
They were very bad but, I
was the only one doing them.

00:09:25.466 --> 00:09:28.217
So, a lot of friends, when
I was doing my short films.

00:09:28.217 --> 00:09:30.168
They would see the effect and say,

00:09:30.168 --> 00:09:31.001
"Who did that for you?"

00:09:31.001 --> 00:09:32.349
And I say, "I did it."

00:09:32.349 --> 00:09:35.173
and they started telling
me, "Would you do mine?"

00:09:35.173 --> 00:09:38.455
and I started doing it
and I realized it was

00:09:38.455 --> 00:09:42.248
an edge with which going to feature films.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.595
And what I did is, for
example, we did a TV series

00:09:45.595 --> 00:09:48.856
called La Hora Marcada,
which is terrible film making

00:09:48.856 --> 00:09:50.344
but, we were all learning.

00:09:50.344 --> 00:09:54.647
Alfonso Cuarón was there, I
was there and Manuel Evescue,

00:09:54.647 --> 00:09:56.997
the DP, Guillermo Navarro, my DP.

00:09:56.997 --> 00:09:59.648
All of us started in
that series and we were

00:09:59.648 --> 00:10:03.249
doing little experiments
and I said to the producers,

00:10:03.249 --> 00:10:05.491
"I'll do the make up effects for free,

00:10:05.491 --> 00:10:08.318
"you pay the materials,
I do them for free but,

00:10:08.318 --> 00:10:12.245
"in exchange I write and I write episodes"

00:10:12.245 --> 00:10:13.877
and they said, "That's a good deal."

00:10:13.877 --> 00:10:16.503
So, it was a way to put
your foot in the door and

00:10:16.503 --> 00:10:19.443
I was already on my way to the Cronus.

00:10:19.443 --> 00:10:23.239
I started writing Cronus around 1985 and

00:10:23.239 --> 00:10:27.406
I knew that in order to make
the device, the Cronus device

00:10:29.589 --> 00:10:31.909
and the make up effects, I
needed to create a company

00:10:31.909 --> 00:10:36.022
that would tell the producers
that there's someone

00:10:36.022 --> 00:10:37.171
who can do those effects.

00:10:37.171 --> 00:10:40.805
So, the sooner I did Cronus,
essentially a year later,

00:10:40.805 --> 00:10:44.265
the show was closed because
it had served it's purpose.

00:10:44.265 --> 00:10:46.566
- There's a bunch of
cats who, like I get it,

00:10:46.566 --> 00:10:47.959
they look at him like, this is stupid.

00:10:47.959 --> 00:10:50.489
Why would you waste your
opportunities or something?

00:10:50.489 --> 00:10:53.320
They seem to think that this
is something given by others.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:56.363
Like, they still see it as
like, "You've been given

00:10:56.363 --> 00:10:57.196
an opportunity".

00:10:57.196 --> 00:10:58.029
No, nobody gave me Jack.

00:10:58.029 --> 00:11:00.484
I went and created opportunity for myself.

00:11:00.484 --> 00:11:02.331
Nobody ever shows up at
your door, knocks and says,

00:11:02.331 --> 00:11:04.722
"Hey man, you want to tell
stories? Here's a bunch of money.

00:11:04.722 --> 00:11:05.728
Go make pretend"

00:11:05.728 --> 00:11:06.774
That doesn't happen.

00:11:06.774 --> 00:11:08.587
You've got to make steps toward that thing

00:11:08.587 --> 00:11:09.595
in the first place.

00:11:09.595 --> 00:11:12.180
So I spent a lot of time
trying to explain to

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:15.848
people the difference
between given an opportunity

00:11:15.848 --> 00:11:18.087
and creating your world.

00:11:18.087 --> 00:11:19.431
Creating your own opportunity

00:11:19.431 --> 00:11:20.652
because if you create
your own opportunities,

00:11:20.652 --> 00:11:21.654
you'll be owing nobody.

00:11:21.654 --> 00:11:23.535
And then people can't say things like,

00:11:23.535 --> 00:11:24.777
"You shouldn't do this."

00:11:24.777 --> 00:11:25.610
I'm like, "Why?"

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:26.491
As long as I keep my budgets low

00:11:26.491 --> 00:11:28.105
and everybody gets their
money back and stuff,

00:11:28.105 --> 00:11:30.173
I can do whatever goofy
thing I want because,

00:11:30.173 --> 00:11:31.913
I'll tell you right now, I
don't want to go to my grave

00:11:31.913 --> 00:11:34.256
one day being like, "I should
have made the Walrus movie"

00:11:34.256 --> 00:11:35.446
and then drop dead.

00:11:35.446 --> 00:11:36.842
I want to be the guy that's
like, "I can't believe

00:11:36.842 --> 00:11:38.675
we made that Walrus
movie" and then drop dead

00:11:38.675 --> 00:11:41.246
and be satisfied because
then we're talking about

00:11:41.246 --> 00:11:43.708
re-shaping the world or
big important issues.

00:11:43.708 --> 00:11:45.580
Man, this is all micro not macro stuff.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:48.221
It all begins, kind of,
with you so, you know,

00:11:48.221 --> 00:11:49.222
that's about belief.

00:11:49.222 --> 00:11:50.925
You can't expect a bunch
of people out there to

00:11:50.925 --> 00:11:52.217
believe you are this thing unless

00:11:52.217 --> 00:11:53.738
you be this thing yourself

00:11:53.738 --> 00:11:55.104
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:55.104 --> 00:11:56.333
I hope you enjoyed.

00:11:56.333 --> 00:11:58.475
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video

00:11:58.475 --> 00:12:01.037
that you are going to
immediately now apply

00:12:01.037 --> 00:12:03.003
to your life or your business somehow.

00:12:03.003 --> 00:12:04.669
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:12:04.669 --> 00:12:06.110
I'm really curious to find out.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:08.084
I also want to give a
shout out to TridentLion.

00:12:08.084 --> 00:12:10.104
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:10.104 --> 00:12:13.294
Your One Word, and reading
it and doing a review

00:12:13.294 --> 00:12:14.377
on your You Tube channel.

00:12:14.377 --> 00:12:16.752
I really, really
appreciate the support and

00:12:16.752 --> 00:12:18.414
I'm so glad that you enjoyed the book.

00:12:18.414 --> 00:12:23.084
- [Narrator] Today this video
is all about Your One Word.

00:12:23.084 --> 00:12:25.288
- Thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:25.288 --> 00:12:26.427
I believe in you.

00:12:26.427 --> 00:12:29.307
I hope you continue to be
in yourself and whatever

00:12:29.307 --> 00:12:30.524
your one word is.

00:12:30.524 --> 00:12:32.941
Much love. I'll see you soon.

